enchilada: BT: real WCN3990 on QUP SE6 UART, staged behind btreal=1/2/3 (probe, power + version, firmware)

PLAN-ENCHILADA.md §8 steps 3-6. New bsd/dev/sweet_btq.c, started from sweet_bt_init() (btfake is
unchanged: the iOS stack keeps the fake controller), only with rpmhrsc=0x179e0000; a kernel thread
waits 30 s, then each stage ends in "SWEET BTQ: stage N: ..." and anything unexpected in "stage N:
STOP ...". btreal=1 only reads: GCC 0x5200c and the wrap_0 m/s-AHB + wrap0_s6 CBCRs, the s6 RCG
0x17754 (DFS enable and levels), GPLL0, TLMM gpio45-48 (EAST), cmd-db ldoa5/7/17/25/23 + rfclka2
(new read-only sweet_rpmh_addr), and the SE6 (0x898000) / QUP0 registers only if their clocks
already run. btreal=2 writes, in Linux's order: gpio45-48 to qup6 with the sdm845.dtsi
qup_uart6_4pin bias, GCC vote bits 6/7/16 (read-modify-write) and the RCG to 7.3728 MHz
(GPLL0_OUT_EVEN M/N 384/15625 as clk_rcg2 shared set_rate, or a DFS level through CLK_SEL), the SE
as qcom_geni_serial port_setup (FIFO, polled, SE_IRQ_EN 0), the WCN3990 rails and RF_CLK2 through
0267's sweet_rpmh_wlan_power() (Linux's DT voltages), power pulses 0xC0 @2400 and 0xFC @115200 with
flow control off, port reopen, then EDL 0x19 on 0xfc00, logging product/SoC/ROM/patch (hci_qca.c,
btqca.c). btreal=3 reads crbtfw21.tlv and crnv21.bin from bluetooth_a (UFS LUN 4 via 0260; offsets,
sizes and crc32 in the FAT16 image sha256 fe481f68...), sends 0xfc48 0x11 and moves the host to
3.2 Mbaud (102.4 MHz / 1), sends both files as 243-byte EDL 0x1e segments (NVM tags as btqca.c sets
them, already so in this file), HCI_Reset and Read_Local_Version (manufacturer 29). Rails and
clocks are never voted off; at the end RX stops and RFR is held not ready.

